 HISTORY                                                          3052 1451
 -------                                                          3052 1451
 This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction Physics  3052 1451
 (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University, USA. The        3052 1451
 inelastic thermal scattering law data for Al2O3 (sapphire) was   3052 1451
 developed using the ab-initio lattice dynamics methods [1]. The  3052 1451
 Full Law Scattering System Hub (FLASSH) was used to generate     3052 1451
 MF=7 data for Al in Al2O3 with mass and free atom cross          3052 1451
 sections as shown below [2]. Sapphire is typically used as a     3052 1451
 single crystal neutron filter, whereby elastic scattering is     3052 1451
 negligible [3]. This library, therefore, contains only           3052 1451
 inelastic scattering data (MT = 4).                              3052 1451
                                                                  3052 1451
